.024087198078632355, 0.025578906992450356]], "latencies": [1.4810972979757935, 8.842537865974009, 2.434226304059848, 2.5048161789309233, 1.2483133400091901, 8.17221885395702, 0.22959910903591663, 0.33610293606761843], "start_times": [785469.554493367, 785471.035875979, 785479.878692445, 785482.313266544, 785484.818367297, 785486.066929147, 785494.239394504, 785494.469304691], "queue_times": [9.903393220156431e-05, 1.481468933983706, 10.324279882013798, 12.758850167971104, 15.26394569594413, 16.512504308950156, 24.684966812026687, 24.91487412492279], "generated_texts": ["Yes, I\u2019m familiar", "Below is a **complete, ready\u2011to\u2011run Rust project** that\n\n1. Reads the current clipboard text (Windows, macOS, Linux).\n2. Sends that text to the ElevenLabs TTS API.\n3. Streams the returned MP3/OGG audio to your speakers.\n\n> **TL;DR**  \n> ```bash\n> cargo run --release\n> ```\n\n---\n\n## 1. Project layout\n\n```\nelevenlabs-tts/\n\u251c\u2500 Cargo.toml\n\u2514\u2500 src/\n   \u2514\u2500 main.rs\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. Prerequisites\n\n| Item | How to get it |\n|------|---------------|\n| **ElevenLabs API key** | Sign up at <https://elevenlabs.io>, go to *API* \u2192 *API Key*. |\n| **Voice ID** | You can use the default voice (`\"EXAVITQu4vr4xnSDxMaL\"`) or fetch your own via the API. |\n| **Rust toolchain** | `rustup install stable` (or use the latest stable). |\n| **Audio output** | Any working audio device (the `rodio` crate uses the default output device). |\n\n---\n\n## 3. `Cargo.toml`\n\n```toml\n[package]\nname = \"elevenlabs-tts\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\nedition = \"2021\"\n\n[dependencies]\n# Clipboard access (cross\u2011platform)\narboard = \"3.2\"\n\n# HTTP client\nreqwest = { version = \"0.12\", features = [\"json\", \"stream\"] }\n\n# Async runtime\ntokio = { version = \"1\", features = [\"full\"] }\n\n# JSON (de)serialization\nserde = { version = \"1.0\", features = [\"derive\"] }\nserde_json = \"1.0\"\n\n# Audio playback\nrodio = \"0.17\"\n\n# Error handling\nanyhow = \"1.0\"\n\n# Environment variable loading\ndotenvy = \"0.15\"\n```\n\n> **Why these crates?**  \n> *`arboard`* is a small, pure\u2011Rust clipboard library that works on all major OSes.  \n> *`reqwest`* is the de\u2011facto HTTP client for Rust.  \n> *`rodio`* can play raw audio streams or files.  \n> *`dotenvy`* lets you keep your API key out of the source code", "Sure thing! To make the \u201cFilters\u201d section clearer and easier to read, I\u2019ll need the current version of the document (or at least the part that contains the Filters). Could you paste the text you\u2019d like me to reformat? Once I have that, I\u2019ll produce a \u201csecond draft\u201d with", "", "", "Below is a **complete, end\u2011to\u2011end recipe** for building a tiny \u201cdummy\u2011data\u201d CRUD app with:\n\n| Layer | Tech | What it does |\n|-------|------|--------------|\n| **Backend** | Node\u202f+\u202fExpress | REST API that stores data in memory (or a JSON file) |\n| **Frontend** | React (Vite) | UI that lets you create, read, update & delete dummy items |\n| **Build** | Vite \u2192 `dist/` | Production\u2011ready static bundle |\n| **Deploy** | 3 options \u2013 Heroku, Vercel, Docker | Pick the one that fits your stack |\n\n> **Why this stack?**  \n> * Express is the de\u2011facto Node web framework.  \n> * Vite gives you lightning\u2011fast dev & a tiny build.  \n> * The same repo can be deployed to a PaaS or containerised \u2013 no extra plumbing.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Project layout\n\n```\ndummy-app/\n\u251c\u2500 backend/\n\u2502  \u251c\u2500 src/\n\u2502  \u2502  \u251c\u2500 routes/\n\u2502  \u2502  \u2502  \u2514\u2500 dummy.js\n\u2502  \u2502  \u251c\u2500 data.js\n\u2502  \u2502  \u2514\u2500 server.js\n\u2502  \u251c\u2500 package.json\n\u2502  \u2514\u2500 .env\n\u251c\u2500 frontend/\n\u2502  \u251c\u2500 src/\n\u2502  \u2502  \u251c\u2500 components/\n\u2502  \u2502  \u2502  \u251c\u2500 DummyForm.jsx\n", "", ""], "errors": ["", "", "", "", "", 